// c05_reserved_word_as_name.exsc
//
// Case c05. The mistake: `firma per: u64 = a;` -- `per` (reserved, §8.4
// iteration group) used as a binding name.
//
// Review reported: `2:11 EXS-E0220` + fix `per_` -- then 3 more
// diagnostics, ending in a bogus `EXS-E0203 unexpected end of input`
// demanding a `}` in a brace-balanced file. Verdict: "bad" -- the primary
// diagnostic and fix are correct, but 3 spurious follow-on diagnostics
// appear, one of which (the final EXS-E0203) is actively wrong: the file's
// braces are balanced.
//
// Reconstruction: byte-faithful. Counting from the first byte of `publica`
// below, this file reproduces the primary `2:11 EXS-E0220` with fix
// `replace -> "per_"`, followed by exactly 3 more diagnostics, the last of
// which is `EXS-E0203 unexpected end of input` with a fix inserting `}` at
// EOF -- even though this file's two `{`/two `}` are balanced. Matches the
// review's description exactly, including the "bogus" follow-on.

publica functio maxima(a: u64) -> u64 {
    firma per: u64 = a;
    redde per;
}
